  (text "12.2 kHz" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 198.12 86.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "6ba69d32-00f1-57b7-ba2e-e44054637ba5"))
  (text "Section 7 of the circuit notes. The pedal's EQ circuit is not public; the DSP uses digital filters (fi.peak_eq_cq,\nfi.high_shelf, fi.lowpass), and this sheet is a standard analogue realisation of them, all chosen.\nBass: graphic-EQ boost/cut band, 110 Hz, Q 0.9, +/-12 dB (bassF, bassQ). LX1, LX2 are simulated inductors (gyrators).\nScoop: fixed -6 dB notch at 350 Hz, Q 0.7 (scoopF, scoopQ, scoopDB), reported by measurement [6].\nTreble: a first-order shelf with the same pot arrangement; the DSP's shelf is third-order, so it is steeper.\nRX21, CX9: fixed 12 kHz low-pass (topLP) so a full treble boost peaks broadly in the upper treble." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 198.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid "4f10a666-64ff-572e-a97d-8a8eb2935555"))
